We recall the following sieve estimate (see, for example, \cite[Theorem 7.11]{MontgomeryVaughan}): For $u>1+1/(\log{Y})^{1/2}$

\begin{equation}
\#\{n<Y:\,p|n\Rightarrow p\ge Y^{1/u}\}=(\omega(u)+o_u(1))\frac{u Y}{\log{Y}},
\label{eq:Buchstab}
\end{equation}

where $\omega(u)$ is the Buchstab function defined by the delay-differential equation

\begin{align*}
\qquad\omega(u)&=1/u, &&1\le u\le 2,\qquad\\
\omega'(u)&=\omega(u-1)-\omega(u), &&u>2.
\end{align*}

