\label{lmm:LatticeApprox}

Let $\delta>0$ and $X,N,K\ge1$ be such that $\delta\ge N/X$. Let $\mathcal{B}_1=\mathcal{B}_1(N,K,\delta)\subseteq[0,X)^2$ be the set of pairs $(a_1,a_2)\in\mathbb{Z}^2$ such that there is a lattice $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{Z}^3$ of rank 2 such that
\[\#\{\mathbf{n}\in\Lambda:\,| n_1a_1+n_2a_2+n_3 X|\le \delta X,\,\|\mathbf{n}\|_2\le N\}\ge  \delta K N^2,\]
and moreover the points counted above do not all lie on a line through the origin.

Then all pairs $(a_1,a_2)\in\mathcal{B}_1$ have the simultaneous rational approximations

\begin{align*}
\frac{a_1}{X}&=\frac{b_1}{q}+O\Bigl(\frac{1}{N K q}\Bigr),\\
\frac{a_2}{X}&=\frac{b_2}{q}+O\Bigl(\frac{1}{N K q}\Bigr),
\end{align*}

for some integer $q\ll X/N K$.

\begin{align*}
